    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1">

                <pb facs="0095" n="1" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg1"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.60d4/6</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Finland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Pearson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Helsingfors</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-03-08">March 8, 1930</date>.<lb/>[Received April
                        1.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1597</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to the
                    Department’s Instruction No. 134 of September 21, 1929,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d1-f1"/> and to previous correspondence, concerning the conclusion
                    of a Naturalization Treaty between the United States and Finland, and to enclose
                    herewith a copy of a note received from the Foreign Office dated March 7, 1930,
                    setting forth the Finnish Government’s views and making certain suggestions for
                    modifications in the draft treaty which was forwarded with the Department’s
                    Instruction No. 99 of December 1, 1928.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d1-f2"/></p>
                <p>The Legation will await the Department’s further instructions.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alfred J. Pearson</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d1-a1.xml" xpointer="d1-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
